          <div id="znid-362777487868"
            class="zn-element-wrapper 
                
              " 
            data-type="text"
            
          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Mayland Earth to Sky Park brings the universe a little closer to home. This International Dark Sky Park near Burnsville is home to the Bare Dark Sky Observatory and the Sam Scope, a 34-inch Newtonian telescope with a mirror wide enough to make distant planets, stars, and other celestial wonders look downright neighborly.</p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;"><br></span></p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;">During monthly Community Viewing Nights, astronomers guide visitors through two hours of skywatching with the Sam Scope and a smaller 14-inch planetary telescope. Space is limited, and tickets tend to disappear faster than a shooting star, so reservations are required.</span></p></div>
            </div>
            
            
          </div>
        

          <div id="znid-578953093561"
