              " 
            data-type="text"
            
          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Cherry Springs State Park is to stargazers what Dollywood is to Dolly fans: hallowed ground. Sitting about 2,300 feet above sea level and surrounded by the Susquehannock State Forest, the park is protected from much of the artificial light produced by nearby towns and cities.</p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;"><br></span></p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;">Casual observers can use the Night Sky Public Viewing Area, while serious astronomers can reserve space in the overnight Astronomy Observation Field, a dedicated viewing area with concrete telescope pads and electrical hookups. The park also hosts public programs throughout the year for folks who cannot tell Cassiopeia from a casserole.</span></p></div>
