              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Pisgah National Forest, North Carolina&nbsp;</p></div>
            </div>
            
            
          </div>
        

          <div id="znid-642912769679"
            class="zn-element-wrapper 
                
              " 
            data-type="text"
            
          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Black Balsam Knob has no planetarium, public telescope, or astronomer pointing out the constellations. What it does have is a 6,214-foot summit, a wide-open grassy bald, and very little standing between visitors and the heavens.</p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;"><br></span></p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;">A trail of less than a mile climbs from the parking area to the summit. Because the mountaintop is largely free of trees, stargazers get broad views in nearly every direction. If you are feeling adventurous, haul in a tent.</span></p></div>
            </div>
            
            
          </div>
        

