              " 
            data-type="text"
            
          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Pickett CCC Memorial State Park sits in a remote corner of the Cumberland Plateau, where light pollution has not yet crashed the party. Pickett and the neighboring Pogue Creek Canyon State Natural Area earned International Dark Sky Park status in 2015, protecting more than 19,000 acres of seriously starry real estate.</p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;"><br></span></p><p><span style="color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit;">For the best view, head to the Pogue Creek Canyon Astronomy Field, a purpose-built clearing with an unobstructed view of the night sky. Once the stars have thoroughly worn you out, retreat to a campsite or historic cabin for some well-earned shut-eye.</span></p></div>
